{"authored" [{"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{x+1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "027204b3cbdf3a65f7eb179b07ae00d638522aef9bb0c783f1db77ebff526c31" "basis" 1158 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "027204b3cbdf3a65f7eb179b07ae00d638522aef9bb0c783f1db77ebff526c31" "basis" 1158 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "46dbe064e7d548bc283b07a09958fc59b77b8700062f68f20f01d2ba9a3bc5eb" "basis" 1158 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-154678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "027204b3cbdf3a65f7eb179b07ae00d638522aef9bb0c783f1db77ebff526c31" "basis" 1158 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "027204b3cbdf3a65f7eb179b07ae00d638522aef9bb0c783f1db77ebff526c31" "basis" 1158 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-158027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012237/state.json" "file_sha256" "027204b3cbdf3a65f7eb179b07ae00d638522aef9bb0c783f1db77ebff526c31" "basis" 1158