\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{y}^{3}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-158025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "{2}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}"] ["math" "{2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}"] ["math" "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-118885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "4{e}^{y}={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y}=2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2y}=x+C"] ["math" "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-154373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+K"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"