ifferential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)=x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+C)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+1)+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-158017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+{e}^{{x}^{3}}+K"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-3854" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y+3y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+x}}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+2x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-14247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y}=2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=({x}^{2}+x)^{2}"] ["math" "y=({x}^{2}+x+C)^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{2})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y}=0$ for $y>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} \\\\ 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-79666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=0$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d742b502ca32641cba777540f1573bb42a081e76ab19f07ca1856c7a2032257a"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/state.json" "file_sha256" "d58261def2f3c1e1a593339f411796a3877b2ddd178081e6b4165119e0748ca4"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $x,y \\geq 0,$ separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{g(y)} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  \\sqrt{2x} \\cdot  \\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041320/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"}] "usage" {"q-157692" [] "e-10849" [] "q-158013" [] "q-8305" [] "q-154359" [] "q-8303" [] "e-10832" [] "q-158027" [] "q-51256" [] "e-10833" [] "q-158035" [] "e-10997" [] "q-14257" [] "q-154373" [] "q-154678" [] "q-14244" [] "q-158026" []} "basis" 1496 "retractions" [[17592186068986 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y^{\\prime } = y\\sin x$ for $y \\ne 0$."] [17592186068986 :question/worked-solution "Because $y\\ne0$, separate and integrate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{y}=\\sin x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|=-\\cos x+C.$$\nExponentiating and absorbing the sign into a nonzero constant gives $y=Ke^{-\\cos x}$, with $K\\ne0$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186065711 17592186065712 17592186065713 17592186065714 17592186065715 17592186065717 17592186065718 17592186065719 17592186065720 17592186065721 17592186065813 17592186065814 17592186065815 17592186065816 17592186065817 17592186065831 17592186065832 17592186065833 17592186065834 17592186065835 17592186065849 17592186065850 17592186065851 17592186065852 17592186065853 17592186068286 17592186068287 17592186068288 17592186068289 17592186068290 17592186068292 17592186068293 17592186068294 17592186068295 17592186068296 17592186290022 17592186290023 17592186290024 17592186290025 17592186290026 17592186290043 17592186290044 17592186290045 17592186290046 17592186290047 17592186290078 17592186290079 17592186290080 17592186290081 17592186290082 17592186290085 17592186290086 17592186290087 17592186290088 17592186290089 17592186290092 17592186290093 17592186290094 17592186290095 17592186290096 17592186295232 17592186295233 17592186295234 17592186295235 17592186295236] "immutable_fields" [[17592186065710 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065710 :answer-field/id] [17592186065710 :answer-field/key] [17592186065710 :answer-field/type] [17592186065716 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065716 :answer-field/id] [17592186065716 :answer-field/key] [17592186065716 :answer-field/type] [17592186065812 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065812 :answer-field/id] [17592186065812 :answer-field/key] [17592186065812 :answer-field/type] [17592186065830 :a